From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:13:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] test(claude-eval): G262-8 bounded refusal of the passage
 projection budget

The budgets now bound the chunking itself (chunk_messages max_chunks), so
a tiny max_points no longer materialises a whole large archive before
refusing (180 kchars: 66 ms to 3 ms; 1 Mchars: 423 ms to 6 ms, no chunk
returned). Same bytes re-projected: no chunking. The canonical read stays
whole (needed for the digest). Whitespace chunks may make a refusal
conservative, never permissive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rv89UzspoLREq2u9UkZssh
